WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.030 --> 00:00:05.540
We've finally got the first trailer for Aquaman
and let's just say I'm digging it!

00:00:05.540 --> 00:00:09.860
Yippee-ki-yay, movie lovers, it's Jan here
and today I'm breaking down the top five moments

00:00:09.860 --> 00:00:13.339
and easter eggs in the epic Comic Con trailer
for Aquaman.

00:00:13.339 --> 00:00:16.850
And just before we start, if you're new here,
be sure to subscribe to stay up-to-date with

00:00:16.850 --> 00:00:19.950
all my superhero and Comic Con videos.

00:00:19.950 --> 00:00:24.230
The underwater world of Aquaman that director
James Wan will be bringing to the big screen

00:00:24.230 --> 00:00:25.390
looks pretty breath-taking.

00:00:25.390 --> 00:00:28.040
"Welcome home."

00:00:28.040 --> 00:00:29.360
"Badass!"

00:00:29.360 --> 00:00:38.650
"My brother has come from the surface!"

00:00:38.650 --> 00:00:43.539
Comic book fans will likely be extremely happy
at the level of comic book accuracy, and the

00:00:43.539 --> 00:00:46.239
world-building going on here is fantastic.

00:00:46.239 --> 00:00:51.249
For example, those sharks and sea dragons
with their riders are amazing to see in action.

00:00:51.249 --> 00:00:55.559
And jumping ahead in the trailer, we have
to talk about the incredible awesomeness of

00:00:55.559 --> 00:00:57.750
the underwater war that's teased.

00:00:57.750 --> 00:01:06.079
"I'm bringing the wrath of the Seven Seas
with me."

00:01:06.079 --> 00:01:09.580
Let's just go back over the epicness of it
all to check the details.

00:01:09.580 --> 00:01:13.450
Behind that huge school of sharks advancing,
there's some tentacled craft that look a bit

00:01:13.450 --> 00:01:16.399
like squids or they may be octopus-inspired.

00:01:16.399 --> 00:01:21.039
And as they advance on the army of giant crab
and lobster-like creatures, I love the way

00:01:21.039 --> 00:01:26.460
these giant alligators or tylosaurs swim in
and go in for the kill on one of the crustaceans.

00:01:26.460 --> 00:01:29.759
Talking of battles, Black Manta looks amazing.

00:01:29.759 --> 00:01:36.229
"The war is coming to the surface and I am
bringing the wrath of the Seven Seas with

00:01:36.229 --> 00:01:37.229
me."

00:01:37.229 --> 00:01:40.659
This is a very comic book accurate costume
for this second villain and James Wan has

00:01:40.659 --> 00:01:44.570
said that the movie will reveal how Black
Manta got his costume and how he can shoot

00:01:44.570 --> 00:01:47.369
plasma beams out of his bug-eyed helmet.

00:01:47.369 --> 00:01:51.740
The actor who plays him has said Black Manta
is simply out for revenge on Aquaman and he's

00:01:51.740 --> 00:01:55.100
not planning to take over the world or anything
like that.

00:01:55.100 --> 00:01:58.409
From the trailer, it looks like the cause
of Black Manta's grievance against Arthur

00:01:58.409 --> 00:02:03.499
Curry will be when Aquaman attacks a submarine
that he's hijacked with some other mercenaries.

00:02:03.499 --> 00:02:08.280
By the way, it looks like Black Manta will
be used as a pawn by Aquaman's main villain,

00:02:08.280 --> 00:02:11.830
Arthur's brother Orm, who wants to bring war
to the surface world.

00:02:11.830 --> 00:02:16.380
There's a glimpse of that when Black Manta
wreaks havoc with his laser eyes on a town's

00:02:16.380 --> 00:02:17.380
rooftops.

00:02:17.380 --> 00:02:21.680
Right, let's go back to the water for yet
another visual feast when Aquaman and Mera

00:02:21.680 --> 00:02:23.910
encounter creatures from the Trench.

00:02:23.910 --> 00:02:28.180
James Wan is a master of horror movies and
these moments are an homage to the type of

00:02:28.180 --> 00:02:31.599
scary monsters in Creature From The Black
Lagoon.

00:02:31.599 --> 00:02:35.890
This is a scene where the Trench people attack
a boat to kill and eat the people on board

00:02:35.890 --> 00:02:40.900
and it looks like Aquaman and Mera are using
a flare to draw or scare them away.

00:02:40.900 --> 00:02:44.790
The visual look of this scene is stunning
and the way the creatures swarm into the ocean

00:02:44.790 --> 00:02:48.690
like a horde of ants to chase after Aquaman
and Mera is epic.

00:02:48.690 --> 00:02:52.670
The filmmakers have said the Trench people
are like "the mole people of the sea".

00:02:52.670 --> 00:02:56.970
They don't actually have any eyes, so I'm
curious to find out exactly how the flare

00:02:56.970 --> 00:02:59.300
works to draw them away from the boat.

00:02:59.300 --> 00:03:03.790
By the way, I'm also getting a touch of Alien
xenomorph vibes from one of the close-up shots

00:03:03.790 --> 00:03:06.349
of the Trench creatures in the footage.

00:03:06.349 --> 00:03:10.250
And if you enjoyed the theme in the trailer,
you might not have realised that it's actually

00:03:10.250 --> 00:03:14.970
a cool musical easter egg to Batman v Superman,
specifically the trailer for the Ultimate

00:03:14.970 --> 00:03:15.970
Edition.

00:03:15.970 --> 00:03:20.459
So, overall, I really dug this trailer, but
I'm not totally sure about some of the corny

00:03:20.459 --> 00:03:21.459
one-liners.

00:03:21.459 --> 00:03:24.180
"That was the worst pep talk.

00:03:24.180 --> 00:03:25.180
Ever."

00:03:25.180 --> 00:03:26.180
Though some of them are probably gonna be
crowd-pleasers.

00:03:26.180 --> 00:03:27.900
"Permission to come aboard?"

00:03:27.900 --> 00:03:28.900
"We're here."

00:03:28.900 --> 00:03:30.780
"What are you doing?"

00:03:30.780 --> 00:03:32.220
"Wait, wait, wait!"

00:03:32.220 --> 00:03:34.209
"She hasn't a parachute!"

00:03:34.209 --> 00:03:36.950
"Redheads, you gotta love 'em."

00:03:36.950 --> 00:03:41.470
Also, some of the green screen was a bit noticeable
in a few sequences, but that's pretty normal

00:03:41.470 --> 00:03:46.340
at this stage and VFX are often improved between
trailer releases and the final theatrical

00:03:46.340 --> 00:03:48.689
release, so hopefully that's the case here
too.

00:03:48.689 --> 00:03:51.489
So, what do you think about the Aquaman trailer?

00:03:51.489 --> 00:03:53.930
And what were the best moments for you?

00:03:53.930 --> 00:03:57.939
Let's discuss more in the comments and do
leave a like if you enjoyed this video.

